  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 AM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nDry, stable air over the eastern two-thirds of the CWA and upper \nhigh in NE NM will inhibit storms over the lowlands late this \nafternoon and into the evening. A storm or 2 could form over the \nSacs but will have a hard time making it off of them. Looks like a\nrepeat of yesterday out west where widely scattered to scattered \nstorms will develop by mid afternoon and move out of the area in \nthe early evening. Expect another mild night with most lows in the\n70s/60s mountains. Little change in the pattern for Thu with high\ntemps over the lowlands reaching 102-107. NBM temps looked a \ndegree or two low and did raise up, especially along RGV to line \nup with the ongoing Heat Advisory. \n\nGoing into Fri, the upper high strengthens as it retrogrades into\neastern AZ. GFS showing near a 600dm high developing. H85 temps \nover the lowlands getting into the 36-37C range support highs of \n105-110 for most of the lowlands. Thinking the Heat Advisory will \nneed to be expanded in coverage for Fri afternoon. Again did raise\nhighs from NBM, closer to the MAV which came in with 109 for ELP \nand 106 for LRU. Didn't go quite that hot at ELP, but it's not out\nof the question. As the upper high shifts west, we start to get a\nreturn of some moisture coming around the ridge. Thunderstorm \nchances will spread across most of the area Fri with generally low\nscattered coverage for the lowlands going into the evening. \nSaturday is looking like the most interesting day with best \nmoisture and instability around. Scattered lowland to numerous \nstorm coverage in the mountains is expected. This far out, I did \nlower NBM PoPs a little bit from the 80s in the Sacs and went with\n60-70%. With the NE flow and GFS showing LI's of -4 to -5C over \nthe east, could see a few severe storms. Temperatures will cool \ndown a little bit here with highs closer to 100 for the lowlands.\n\nMore stable air moves in for Sunday with storm coverage back to \nstaying out west with temps another couple degrees cooler than \nSat. The upper high weakens over AZ for early next week with daily\ndisturbances moving around the high and bringing mountain storms \nwhich will push outflows onto the lowlands and isolated \nthunderstorm coverage. Temps will start to rebound a bit but look \nto stay below advisory criteria.",
